cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "kisscrit: critical configurations of the min-distance (kissing / Tammes) function on spheres"
abstract: >-
  Research code for the critical configurations of the kissing / Tammes function of N points on
  the sphere, and for the computation towards completeness of the N = 12 census above r = 1.
  Research snapshot: the completeness of the N = 12 census above r = 1 is not established;
  STATUS.md in the repository says what is proved, computed and assumed.
authors:
  - family-names: Kusner
    given-names: Wöden
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wkusner/kisscrit"
keywords:
  - kissing configurations
  - Tammes problem
  - critical points
  - interval arithmetic
